WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.971
A punk-rock Isabela, a secret room for Luisa,
and missing magical characters are just some

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:10.340
of the fascinating scenes and storylines cut
from the final version of Encanto.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.910
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything you never

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.000
got to see in Disney's Encanto!

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.800
A few spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.860
Although Isabela can conjure beautiful plants
and flowers out of thin air, a fun idea for

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.180
her which didn't make it into the movie was
the ability to create animated plant creatures,

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.130
such as these potato characters.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.630
The idea was that there would have been a
little potato family living in the house,

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:38.680
tending to crops, and decked out in traditional
outfits.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.920
Isabela was designed with a classic Disney
princess look and vibe to reflect her role

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.950
as the family's golden child.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.079
As the story progresses though, she reveals
that being a Señorita Perfecta isn't what

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:53.900
she really wants and she transforms her look
from soft pastel shades to bolder colours.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.829
However, the filmmakers also considered a
punk-rock version of Isabela that hinted at

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:00.640
an even edgier vibe, though it didn't make
it into the final film.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.160
In the movie, among the expectations placed
on Isabela is that she should marry Mariano,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.580
her picture-perfect male equivalent.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.970
But originally her suitor was going to be
someone quite different, a guy from the city

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.020
called Bubo.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.280
He had a modern look that contrasted with
the traditional feel of the Encanto villagers,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.360
and he would have brought a comedic tone to
his scenes with a fish-out-of-water vibe and

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.159
dorky personality.

00:01:23.159 --> 00:01:26.990
Another entertaining piece of concept art
which wasn't in the movie is this humorous

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:33.119
moment of Isabela imitating Mirabel with a
pair of green glasses created from her vines.

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:37.130
Although each family member has a room of
their own reflecting their gift and personality,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.780
we never actually get to see inside Luisa's
room.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.750
Concept art from The Art of Encanto book reveals
an early idea for her room was that it should

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.810
be made entirely of stone to reflect her strength
and the fact she's the most responsible person

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.930
in the family.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:56.000
The overall idea was that it should look very
boring, except for a secret door in the room

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.430
that only Luisa knew about which led to a
theme park where she "could just have fun

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.280
like a little kid", and escape the pressures
of her family duties.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:09.580
Some other versions of her room include various
locations set up as training areas for exercising

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.719
and weights for her to practise lifts.

00:02:11.719 --> 00:02:15.790
Unfortunately, the closest we got to this
in the film was a snippet of Luisa running

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.329
on a magical treadmill created by the casita
during the opening song, "The Family Madrigal".

00:02:20.329 --> 00:02:25.849
Although there are plenty of magical characters
in the final film, early concept art reveals

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:28.739
a number of deleted characters we never got
to see.

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:33.279
Two characters who were scrapped from the
script were magical twins Amélia and Sofía

00:02:33.279 --> 00:02:38.279
who were inseparable, but during their 15th
birthday celebration they "unleashed blinding

00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:40.470
auras over their guests."

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:44.639
Amélia's aura contained all the beauty the
twins had collected inside since they were

00:02:44.639 --> 00:02:47.049
born and the crowd fell in love with her.

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:52.999
By contrast, Sofía released all their ugliness,
sparking a feeling of revulsion towards her.

00:02:52.999 --> 00:02:57.439
This traumatic event drove a wedge between
the sisters that would take decades to be

00:02:57.439 --> 00:02:58.439
undone.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:02.919
There was also a pool-playing fortune teller
character who has a similar look and trickster

00:03:02.919 --> 00:03:04.019
vibe to Camilo.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:08.309
And then there was Zoe who could speak to
and connect with machines, getting them to

00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:10.489
repair themselves whenever they were broken.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:15.029
However, when she was asleep or took a siesta,
the machines would also shut down and refuse

00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:16.249
to work.

00:03:16.249 --> 00:03:19.879
This family portrait also reveals more deleted
characters.

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:25.480
Behind Mirabel is an angry-looking girl called
Fuega who has some kind of fire powers, something

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.359
some fans speculated Anna might have in the
Frozen sequel.

00:03:29.359 --> 00:03:34.169
From the art, it feels like Fuega's gift of
fire was triggered in some way by her emotions,

00:03:34.169 --> 00:03:36.519
similar to Pepa and her weather powers.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.239
And in this version Pepa had a twin called
Leta who were likely versions of Amélia and

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:43.319
Sofía, who I mentioned before.

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:47.849
There's also a deleted character called Princesa,
and it looks like her princess vibe ended

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:51.010
up being merged with Isabela's flower powers.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:55.529
Standing next to Agustín is a woman named
Miranda who's holding a bunny implying she

00:03:55.529 --> 00:03:59.469
had a connection to animals, similar to Antonio
in the final film.

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:04.779
And given she's by Agustín, I think she was
the original version of Mirabel's mother Julieta

00:04:04.779 --> 00:04:07.590
who has the power to heal injuries with food.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:12.739
There's also another older character here
called Raimi in addition to the grumpy Abuela

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:13.739
below.

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:17.660
And there's a short mischievous-looking girl
without a name who wasn't in the final movie

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.660
either.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.540
On top of all that, there's a statue of a
woman wielding a sword whose name is Alejandra.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:28.010
My guess is that this stern-looking character
was the original matriarch who established

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.310
the house and that she was Abuela's mother.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.920
In fact, this fits with the original idea
for Encanto which was that the story "would

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.310
take place over 100 years through multiple
generations".

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:43.450
In terms of Encanto's time period, according
to the filmmakers, the final movie has an

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:48.260
early 1900s look with "a folkloric Colombian
aesthetic", although initially it was going

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:53.260
to have more of a 1950s look like these early
designs for Mirabel.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:58.160
Bruno may be a forbidden word in the Madrigal
family, but Mirabel's mysterious uncle was

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.890
actually originally going to be named Oscar,
as revealed in this colour palette for the

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:03.890
family.

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:08.260
However, according to the Disney Fandom wiki,
Lin Manuel-Miranda changed the name to Bruno

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.250
as he wanted it to fit in the line "We don't
talk about Bruno, no, no, no".

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.350
Given Bruno is initially portrayed as the
black sheep of the family, it's amusing that

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:21.180
Pixar's latest film Luca also had a thing
about Brunos.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.560
Silenzio Bruno!

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.940
Silenzio Bruno!

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.590
Some early designs for Bruno showed him much
younger, and his eyes glowed both green and

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.800
blue, which was a way of playing around with
the idea that he had the ability to see into

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.430
the future.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.710
Another character who changed from her initial
concept is Pepa who controls the weather with

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:39.710
her emotions.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:44.800
Originally, her powers were that she was indestructible
and couldn't get hurt, which made her into

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.470
something of a daredevil.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:51.120
The problem was that her indestructibility
felt too similar to Luisa's great strength,

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.650
so they decided to give her weather-related
powers instead, which kept the sense of eccentricity

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:00.530
and strangeness they were looking for in Mirabel's
aunt.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:05.660
And this version of Antonio had him talking
through his animals and paying them with snacks,

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.190
rather than relaying what they were saying
to him.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.250
Uh huh.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.310
Uh huh.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.910
I understand you.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:16.270
The teaser trailer for Encanto has scenes
which weren't included in the final movie.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.580
There's Luisa doing weights with a pair of
pianos;

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.980
Antonio beckoning, then whistling to call
all his animals to him;

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:27.770
and Isabela swinging down on a vine outside
the house while making flowers around her.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:32.210
I think these scenes were made specifically
for the trailer to show some of the characters'

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.210
powers.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:36.490
There's also what appears to be a deleted
scene in the teaser trailer of Mirabel sitting

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:41.000
on a wall with one of Antonio's tapirs which
I think was a scene cut from just before she

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.140
goes to ask Luisa about what's wrong with
the magic.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:49.410
Although the look and design of the family
home was gorgeous, there were also some fascinating

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:50.820
alternate designs.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:56.240
In this one, the casita was built on top of
some kind of rock formation up in the mountains.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:00.710
The idea was to illustrate how new rooms would
be added onto the house whenever a new family

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.600
member received their gift.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:07.990
Other early designs had the house built around
the natural rocks and boulders in the environment.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:12.330
And this version of the house had no straight
lines to give it an even more whimsical and

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.370
handmade feel.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.822
Another idea for the casita that didn't make
it into the final film was that it

00:07:17.822 --> 00:07:22.590
"was an extension of Abuela […] rather than
the whole family [and] the colour of the wallpaper

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.900
would reflect her mood in whatever room she
was in."

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:30.200
Likewise, in another version of the movie,
as Mirabel narrated the story, the colours

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.730
of the world around her were going to change
according to her emotions.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.580
Then in the third act, the film would have
switched to show "everything from Abuela's

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:43.330
point of view" with things now looking "more
realistic and photographic".

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.910
According to one of the movie's production
designers, that idea was rejected as they

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.370
thought it was "too distracting".

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:54.160
In another rejected storyline, Agustín was
the family patriarch who originally built

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.580
the Madrigal house.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:00.550
In that version, rather than being Julieta's
husband, Agustín was a strong-willed character

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.120
who already had a moustache at the age of
four.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:08.030
He was warned by a mysterious woman against
building a house in the Encanto, and after

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:11.330
he ignored her, the house threw him out the
window.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.990
In Encanto, the characters never leave the
town, so only the magical doors and rooms

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.120
allow them an opportunity to explore other
environments.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.720
However, in an earlier version of the story,
Mirabel went with Abuela to the city the old

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.710
woman originally came from.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:30.650
During the visit, they would have seen technology
not available in the isolated Encanto, including

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.310
the traditional Chiva, colourful buses often
considered symbols of Colombia.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:39.499
And if you want to check out more of the gorgeous
concept art from Encanto, consider getting

00:08:39.499 --> 00:08:41.259
a copy of The Art of Encanto book.

00:08:41.259 --> 00:08:46.290
I've added links in the description on how
you can get the book with free worldwide shipping.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:51.010
So, what do you think of Encanto and do you
wish any of these ideas had been in the final

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.010
movie?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.940
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:58.100
If you enjoyed this, then do like and share
this video, I really appreciate it.

